# React Components

## Component pattern

- Functional components + hooks only. No class components except special cases like `ErrorBoundary`.
- Type props explicitly; prefer `React.ComponentProps<"tag">` for wrapper elements (see `src/components/ui/table.tsx`).
- Named export for shadcn-style components; default export for page components (see `src/pages/not-found/index.tsx`).
- Lazy-load pages with `loadable(() => import("@src/pages/..."))` or `lazyLoad` helper in `src/utils/loadable.tsx`.

## Styling — Tailwind v4 + shadcn

- Always merge classes with `cn()` from `@src/lib/utils` (clsx + tailwind-merge):

```tsx
import { cn } from "@src/lib/utils";

function Spinner({ className, ...props }: React.ComponentProps<"svg">) {
  return <Loader2Icon className={cn("size-4 animate-spin", className)} {...props} />;
}
```

- Use design tokens / CSS variables declared in `src/index.css` (e.g. `bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `border-border`, `bg-muted/50`). Don't hardcode hex if a token exists.
- Dark mode: use `dark:` variant (custom `&:is(.dark *)` configured).
- Icons: `lucide-react`, sizing via Tailwind `size-*`.

## i18n

- Use `useTranslation()` in components; use `translate(...)` from `@src/i18n` in non-component code (interceptor, util).
- Keys are dot-namespaced: `pages.error_boundary.HAVE_PROBLEM`, `commons.ACTIVE`, `error.UNKNOWN_ERROR`.
- Don't hardcode display strings (EN/VI) in JSX for UI text — add keys to `src/i18n/locales/en.json` and `vi.json`.

## Notification

- Use `toast` from `sonner` (`toast.success`, `toast.error`, ...). `<Toaster />` is mounted in `src/main.tsx`.
- Don't use `alert()` or antd `notification` (antd has been removed).
